{"name":"Oak Creek","hex":"#5d504a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Oak Creek","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of streams in the United States.","An unincorporated community known as the Village of Oak Creek, in Yavapai County, Arizona."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Oak_Creek"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oak Creek Canyon","blocks":[{"text":"Oak Creek Canyon is a river gorge located in northern Arizona between the cities of Flagstaff and Sedona. The canyon is often described as a smaller cousin of the Grand Canyon because of its scenic beauty. State Route 89A enters the canyon on its north end via a series of hairpin turns before traversing the bottom of the canyon for about 13 miles (21 km) until the highway enters the town of Sedona."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Oak_Creek_Canyon_02.jpg/330px-Oak_Creek_Canyon_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oak_Creek_Canyon","wikidata":"Q723393"},{"title":"Oak Creek (Owens River tributary)","blocks":[{"text":"Oak Creek is a tributary stream of the Owens River, in Inyo County, California.\nIts mouth lies at an elevation of 3,924 feet / 1,196 meters, 2.2 miles north northwest of Independence, California, just south of the Fort Independence Reservation. Its source is to the west at the foot of the Sierra Nevada at the confluence of South Fork Oak Creek and North Fork Oak Creek at 36°49′57″N 118°15′05″W at an elevation of 4,380 feet / 1,335 meters."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oak_Creek_(Owens_River_tributary)","wikidata":"Q60790468"},{"title":"Oak Creek (Marys River tributary)","blocks":[{"text":"Oak Creek is a tributary, about 3.5 miles (5.6 km) long, of Marys River in Benton County in the U.S. state of Oregon. The stream descends from forested hills north of Corvallis through the northwest part of the city and across the campus of Oregon State University."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Irish_Bend_Covered_Bridge.jpg/330px-Irish_Bend_Covered_Bridge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oak_Creek_(Marys_River_tributary)","wikidata":"Q22954109"},{"title":"Oak","blocks":[{"text":"An oak is a hardwood tree or shrub in the genus Quercus of the beech family. They have spirally arranged leaves, often with lobed edges, and a nut called an acorn, borne within a cup. The genus is widely distributed in the Northern Hemisphere, with some 475 species, both deciduous and evergreen. Fossil oaks date back to the Middle Eocene. Molecular phylogeny shows that the genus is divided into Old World and New World clades, but many oak species hybridise freely, making the genus's history difficult to resolve."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Quercus_robur.jpg/330px-Quercus_robur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oak","wikidata":"Q12004"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Oak_Crk_Canyon.jpg/500px-Oak_Crk_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Oak_Crk_Canyon.jpg/1280px-Oak_Crk_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Oak_Crk_Canyon.jpg/500px-Oak_Crk_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sandstone formation in Oak Creek Canyon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOak_Crk_Canyon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Oak_Creek_Sedona_Arizona.jpg/500px-Oak_Creek_Sedona_Arizona.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Oak_Creek_Sedona_Arizona.jpg/500px-Oak_Creek_Sedona_Arizona.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fishing in Oak Creek, Cathedral Rock in background, 1959.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOak_Creek_Sedona_Arizona.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Brockwell_Oak_%289%29.jpg/120px-Brockwell_Oak_%289%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Brockwell_Oak_%289%29.jpg/250px-Brockwell_Oak_%289%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Brockwell_Oak_%289%29.jpg/120px-Brockwell_Oak_%289%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrockwell_Oak_(9).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Quercus_lusitanica_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-253.jpg/120px-Quercus_lusitanica_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-253.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Quercus_lusitanica_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-253.jpg/250px-Quercus_lusitanica_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-253.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Quercus_lusitanica_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-253.jpg/120px-Quercus_lusitanica_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-253.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQuercus_lusitanica_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-253.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org